From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dwmapi: the accent colour, window attributes, blur behind, transport and timing

- DwmGetColorizationColor failed with E_NOTIMPL: it gives the accent
  Settings keeps (DWM's ColorizationColor, else AccentColor, else the
  Stained Glass purple) and whether transparency is off;
  DwmpGetColorizationParameters, which custom themes read, likewise.
- DwmSetWindowAttribute accepted any attribute with a FIXME. The ones
  that change how DWM would treat the window (non-client rendering
  policy, transitions, peek, Flip3D, iconic representation, freeze,
  border colour, backdrop type...) are checked as Windows checks them and
  kept as window properties; unknown attributes are E_INVALIDARG.
- DwmGetWindowAttribute answered E_NOTIMPL for all but four attributes:
  DWMWA_NCRENDERING_ENABLED (off when the policy disables it),
  DWMWA_CAPTION_BUTTON_BOUNDS and DWMWA_VISIBLE_FRAME_BORDER_THICKNESS
  answer; set-only and unknown ones are E_INVALIDARG.
- DwmEnableBlurBehindWindow failed with E_NOTIMPL (programs then dropped
  their glass windows' alpha); it is kept as a window property.
- DwmGetTransportAttributes said composition was off while
  DwmIsCompositionEnabled says it is on: a local, connected session.
- DwmGetCompositionTimingInfo counts refreshes and frames from the clock
  (they were 0); DwmEnableComposition, DwmEnableMMCSS, DwmDefWindowProc
  and DwmInvalidateIconicBitmaps stop logging FIXMEs for what is right.

Wine's dwmapi test divides by the display frequency, which is 0 under
Xvfb, before and after this patch alike.

Gate: test/dwmattrs-gate.sh (Xvfb). Mutant SG_MUTANT_NO_DWM_ATTRIBUTES
(dwmapi/dwmapi_main.c).
